AllFreqNet: A Unified Frequency-Enhanced All-in-One Framework for Medical Image Restoration

This release is a cleaned distribution of the supplied version3 research code.
The Apache License, Version 2.0 supplied with version3 is retained in LICENSE.
Cleanup changes include UTF-8 formatting, command-line entry points, portable
paths, dataset validation, release documentation, and paper-aligned model class
and file names. Model operations and state_dict parameter names are preserved.

The supplied code is based in part on AMIR:
All-In-One Medical Image Restoration via Task-Adaptive Routing,
Zhiwen Yang et al., MICCAI 2024.
https://github.com/Yaziwel/All-In-One-Medical-Image-Restoration-via-Task-Adaptive-Routing

The Transformer backbone contains components derived from Restormer:
Restormer: Efficient Transformer for High-Resolution Image Restoration,
Syed Waqas Zamir et al., CVPR 2022.
https://github.com/swz30/Restormer
Its MIT license and copyright notice are retained in third_party/Restormer-LICENSE.txt.

The legacy SSIM implementation credits Po-Hsun-Su/pytorch-ssim. The metric
implementation in this release retains its Gaussian-window convention.
https://github.com/Po-Hsun-Su/pytorch-ssim
Its MIT license is retained in third_party/pytorch-ssim-LICENSE.txt.
